# Kbuild is the kernel's own build-description language. The kernel build system reads this
# file to learn what to build. You do not call a compiler yourself.
#
# `obj-m` = "objects built as Modules" (`-m`), as opposed to `obj-y`, which would link the code
# permanently into the kernel image. `hello.o` means "compile `hello.rs` (or `hello.c`) and
# produce the module `hello.ko`".

obj-m := hello.o
